; key_partial_1 -- the P5 positive @key carrier (the partial-binding DAG; there
; was NO positive @key case post-P1, all key_*_1 cases reject at parse). `@key`
; rides on the #local `path` and is read through a DISTINCT bound #query (a
; #query cannot re-declare the #local's name). @key drives the P5
; DeclaredAccessPath model + the -region-out `declared-key` render (pinned via
; the .irgold region step). Since P7 (session 23) it is ALSO the partial-key hash
; SEEK carrier: the bound+free #query lowers to plan=partial-key-hash-seek and an
; Index::First/Next cursor (the `h opt` .irgold step pins the FIRST codegen golden
; since P4 -- the Index<Key19> idx_19 member + the idx_19.First/.Next cursor, no
; NumRows() rescan). The seek is answer-invariant (the full-materialization backend
; answers a complete read), so this .stdout is unchanged across all four
; optimization modes. The DAG STRUCTURE (prefix chain, [A,B]/[B,A]
; convergence) is gated in ctest RegionInstanceP5, not here (a .dr golden cannot
; observe internal schema ids).
#message edge_2(u64 From, u64 To).
#local path(u64 From, u64 To) @key(From).
path(F, T) : edge_2(F, T).
#query reachable_from(bound u64 From, free u64 To) : path(From, To).
